# The ignore file for the LAMBDA image's build, which takes the repository root as its context.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` when one exists and falls back to the context
# root's `.dockerignore` otherwise. That fallback is what this file exists to avoid: the root file
# excludes `lambdas` and `infra` on purpose, to keep them out of the SPA image's context — whose
# build asserts their absence — and a Lambda build reading it would find no source at all.
#
# `apps/portal/Dockerfile` has no sibling ignore file, so the SPA build still reads the root one
# and nothing here reaches it.
#
# Everything the image does not need is excluded rather than merely unused: the context is sent to
# the daemon whole, and `.claude/` alone holds every agent worktree in this checkout.
.git
.github/workflows
.claude
apps
docs
infra
node_modules
**/node_modules
scripts
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/dist
**/coverage
htmlcov
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
